{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\223.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Qulick Check", "conf": 0.795, "box": [[898, 132], [1082, 114], [1086, 151], [902, 169]]}, {"text": " The weight of grade 6 students.", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[248, 157], [763, 136], [764, 181], [250, 202]]}, {"text": " The volume of liquid", "conf": 0.834, "box": [[247, 220], [595, 207], [597, 247], [249, 260]]}, {"text": "The speed of a car", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[965, 260], [1202, 240], [1205, 275], [968, 294]]}, {"text": " The height of a person", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[247, 281], [627, 267], [629, 307], [249, 321]]}, {"text": "The number of cars in a showroom", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[966, 306], [1427, 277], [1429, 317], [968, 346]]}, {"text": "The temperature of a city", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[248, 341], [668, 324], [670, 364], [250, 381]]}, {"text": "The mass of a bag of rice", "conf": 0.877, "box": [[968, 361], [1292, 339], [1295, 375], [971, 397]]}, {"text": "c) Un-grouped data", "conf": 0.845, "box": [[227, 475], [563, 459], [565, 496], [229, 512]]}, {"text": "When data is collected from any source it does not convey to us any meaningful", "conf": 0.915, "box": [[221, 541], [1484, 469], [1486, 518], [223, 590]]}, {"text": "information to understand. This data is called ungrouped data or raw data. Consider the", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[221, 586], [1598, 514], [1601, 569], [223, 641]]}, {"text": "following example.", "conf": 0.895, "box": [[230, 649], [534, 637], [536, 677], [232, 689]]}, {"text": "Example 1:", "conf": 0.872, "box": [[233, 801], [424, 792], [426, 833], [235, 842]]}, {"text": "The temperature in (°C) of a specific city in two weeks is shown below:", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[235, 860], [1321, 800], [1323, 839], [237, 900]]}, {"text": "26°℃", "conf": 0.715, "box": [[1138, 890], [1225, 887], [1226, 930], [1140, 933]]}, {"text": "27℃", "conf": 0.732, "box": [[1275, 886], [1359, 882], [1361, 922], [1277, 926]]}, {"text": "17°℃", "conf": 0.684, "box": [[884, 906], [966, 901], [968, 941], [887, 947]]}, {"text": "34℃", "conf": 0.746, "box": [[1008, 899], [1094, 894], [1096, 935], [1011, 941]]}, {"text": "31℃", "conf": 0.718, "box": [[634, 919], [717, 915], [719, 956], [636, 959]]}, {"text": "16°℃", "conf": 0.667, "box": [[762, 914], [840, 908], [843, 948], [765, 954]]}, {"text": "32°℃", "conf": 0.716, "box": [[504, 926], [588, 921], [591, 962], [507, 968]]}, {"text": "29℃", "conf": 0.725, "box": [[1140, 940], [1226, 937], [1227, 980], [1142, 983]]}, {"text": "21℃", "conf": 0.746, "box": [[1274, 934], [1361, 930], [1363, 973], [1277, 978]]}, {"text": "25℃", "conf": 0.654, "box": [[886, 954], [969, 948], [972, 992], [889, 998]]}, {"text": "35°℃", "conf": 0.684, "box": [[1011, 949], [1093, 944], [1095, 984], [1014, 990]]}, {"text": "33℃", "conf": 0.738, "box": [[636, 969], [718, 963], [720, 1003], [638, 1009]]}, {"text": "24°℃", "conf": 0.599, "box": [[763, 960], [843, 956], [845, 999], [765, 1003]]}, {"text": "23℃", "conf": 0.639, "box": [[506, 976], [590, 969], [593, 1010], [509, 1017]]}, {"text": "We can observe that we cannot come to a quick result after observing this data. This data ", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[241, 1084], [1664, 1012], [1667, 1055], [243, 1127]]}, {"text": "is called ungrouped data. This type of data is difficult to analyse.", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[241, 1148], [1255, 1103], [1257, 1148], [243, 1193]]}, {"text": "d) Grouped data", "conf": 0.872, "box": [[251, 1223], [532, 1207], [534, 1246], [253, 1261]]}, {"text": "When collected data from any source is organised in groups/categories to show some", "conf": 0.956, "box": [[245, 1282], [1590, 1223], [1592, 1273], [247, 1331]]}, {"text": "meaning, this data is called grouped data.", "conf": 0.963, "box": [[250, 1350], [901, 1322], [903, 1368], [252, 1396]]}, {"text": "We can group the above data of temperature (in C) of a city in the following form. .", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[250, 1414], [1560, 1366], [1562, 1416], [252, 1464]]}, {"text": "Draw a table with three columns.", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[257, 1486], [768, 1464], [769, 1504], [259, 1526]]}, {"text": "Divide the temperature of the two weeks into 4 groups.", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[254, 1543], [1113, 1521], [1114, 1576], [256, 1598]]}, {"text": "Number of days when temperature lies between 15 - 20 = 2", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[258, 1612], [1185, 1589], [1186, 1641], [259, 1664]]}, {"text": "Number of days when temperature lies between 21 - 25 = 4", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[260, 1680], [1187, 1660], [1188, 1712], [261, 1732]]}, {"text": "Number of days when temperature lies between 26 - 30 = 3", "conf": 0.968, "box": [[262, 1744], [1188, 1728], [1189, 1784], [263, 1800]]}, {"text": "Number of days when temperature lies between 31 - 35 = 5", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[265, 1810], [1189, 1799], [1190, 1857], [266, 1867]]}, {"text": "class and then organise the data in grouped form.", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[411, 1967], [1038, 1975], [1037, 2019], [411, 2011]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.778, "box": [[364, 2124], [634, 2116], [635, 2150], [365, 2158]]}, {"text": "221", "conf": 0.749, "box": [[917, 2125], [981, 2130], [979, 2168], [914, 2163]]}]}